I have had this issue and solved it by changing the name of the sigma sex effect coefficient in the output to "sig.sex" with the code
model$outStats$parameters[4] <-"sig.sex" where "model" in my model name and [4] was the location of the sigma sex effect coefficient name in the output. After that get.real worked fine.

Jeff

